{
 "lines": [
  {
   "id": "VO-01",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.084,
   "text": "Three friends, same thousand dollars, same day. Twenty years later, one had ten times as much."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-02",
   "start": 6.233,
   "end": 8.484,
   "text": "Wait, how? It's the same money!"
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-03",
   "start": 8.633,
   "end": 15.649,
   "text": "They all bought the S and P five hundred, tiny pieces of five hundred big companies, at the start of two thousand six."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-04",
   "start": 15.748,
   "end": 21.677,
   "text": "Then came the two thousand eight crash, and by year-end, each thousand was worth about seven hundred seventy."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-05",
   "start": 21.776,
   "end": 25.193,
   "text": "Jay sells at year-end and hides the cash in a shoebox."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-06",
   "start": 25.292,
   "end": 31.09,
   "text": "Maya sells too, but buys back at the end of two thousand nine, after missing a twenty-six percent rebound."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-07",
   "start": 31.189,
   "end": 34.348,
   "text": "Sam stays invested and lets his dividends reinvest."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-08",
   "start": 34.744,
   "end": 38.654,
   "text": "At first, Jay feels smart, because shoebox money can't crash."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-09",
   "start": 38.991,
   "end": 46.73,
   "text": "By the end of twenty twenty-five, Jay has seven hundred seventy, Maya about sixty-four hundred, and Sam about eight thousand."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-10",
   "start": 46.829,
   "end": 50.221,
   "text": "Same money, same day, and the friend who stayed in won."
  },
  {
   "id": "VO-11",
   "start": 50.558,
   "end": 54.416,
   "text": "So if your money crashed, would you sell, wait or hold?"
  }
 ],
